 "comparability_statement": "All three approaches now trade the same three assets, SPY/IEF/LQD. AP1 and AP3 form a view on each asset on a one-month horizon; AP2B (JEV) and its within-approach variant AP2A form a single stock-against-bond view on a 12-month horizon and their bond split is a frozen constant from the committed re-specification rather than a decision. Their neutral stock weight is also 60% against 45%, and the systems read different information. Differences in net CER compare complete strategies, including horizon, neutral stance and information access; they are not a controlled comparison of forecasting skill. Results relative to each system's native neutral portfolio do not remove these differences."
